- your name, exactly as it appears on the account;
- your 13-digit Kaskazi account number;
- Kaskazi Bank's international bank identifier code (not available in this demonstration); and
- the name of your branch.

results.answer:
To open a personal Kaskazi account in the app, you need:

- your national ID card or passport;
- your KRA PIN;
- a phone number registered in your name; and
- a selfie taken in the app, which the app compares with the photo on your ID to confirm that the person opening the account is the person on the ID.

If you're opening a Kaskazi Student Account, you also need a valid student ID. Joint and business accounts can't be opened in the app, so those need a branch visit.

sources.quote:
To open any Kaskazi Bank personal account, including the Kaskazi Everyday Account, Kaskazi Goal Saver, Kaskazi Fixed Deposit and Kaskazi Foreign Currency Account, you need:

- your national ID card or passport;
- your KRA PIN;
- a phone number registered in your name; and
- a selfie, if you open the account in the app.

Opening a Kaskazi Bank account in the app usually takes about 10 minutes, but it can take longer if:

- a photo of your ID is blurred, has glare on it or cuts off an edge;
- the names on your ID and KRA PIN don't match exactly;
- the app can't match your selfie to your ID photo, for example in poor light; or
- your phone number turns out not to be registered in your name.

Which rate depends on how much is in the account:

- if your balance is KES 10,000 or more, the whole balance earns 5.0% a year;
- if your balance is below KES 10,000, the whole balance earns 3.0% a year.

